abstract: >-
  This repository contains the implementation, dataset-processing pipeline,
  evaluation scripts, benchmarking utilities, and experimental materials for
  the research project "FD-Net V2: A Scratch-Trained Lightweight Deep Learning
  Architecture for Fabric Defect Diagnosis." The study uses a publicly
  available four-class fabric defect dataset obtained from Roboflow Universe,
  containing Cut, Hole, Stain, and ThreadError categories. The repository
  includes object detection experiments using YOLOv8n, YOLOv8m, RetinaNet,
  and Faster R-CNN, as well as image classification experiments using
  ViT-B/16, VGG16-BN, EfficientNet-B0, FD-Net, and the proposed
  scratch-trained lightweight FD-Net V2. The repository also provides tools
  for processing the original CSV annotations, converting bounding-box
  annotations into YOLO format, generating defect-focused classification
  crops, and benchmarking model computational efficiency.

